// huffTable is one of the thirty-two Huffman tables, as a flat binary tree.
//
// Two entries per node, one per bit. A positive entry is the index of the next node; a negative one
// is a leaf holding both values of the pair, stored as -(x<<4 | y) - 1 so that zero can mean an
// absent branch and the pair (0, 0) is still representable.
